(which allows them he activated without glamour). Iirc Avernian Gates are similar, requiring some specific ritual to open. I do like the blood sacrifice to power it, as a generic deathly thing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how this compared to the ghost binding ceremony in Geist to make a memento. But (now that i read it) that ceremony seem to bind a ghost to their anchor similar to how you describe the above fettered memento... So now i am confused how your object differs (other than being more powerful than the mementos described in the core book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T04:06:32-07:00","id":1519097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1518349-\ud83d\udc7b-new-sin-eater-merits-\u2014-handbook-for-the-recently-deceased-preview#post1518349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the intro: I'm super into Geist and want to inject some life into the line, so I'm making some Storyteller's Vault products to help with that. I've already made <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">a Hunter supplement</a>. Currently I'm juggling three Geist books:<ul><li><i><b>Night Horrors: Unquiet Dead</b></i>, which provides sample NPCs, antagonist and ally. The bulk of it is Geists and Sin-eaters to mix and match, but there's also expanded and clarified rules for Tyrants and sample Krewes, as well as some Ghost Eaters and Reapers.</li> <li><i><b>Book of the Dead: Into the Light</b></i> is a 2e take on a lot of the stuff found in Book of the Dead, including haunted places, River Cities, Dead Dominions, and of course lots of Rivers to drink from.</li> <li>And last is <i><b>Handbook for the Recently Deceased</b></i>, a player's guide that gives alternate ways to play, including a return of Thresholds, different ways to handle archetypes in a more personal way, and Carnivals, Tier 3 krewes.</li> </ul><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd really like to read a 2e take on book of the dead, for night horrors i wanted more necromancers! Love the idea of a powerful Cult of living necromancers abusing the power of death to close off access to the Underworld and how reapers would respond (likely poorly).<br /> <br /> Have a deep dominion in mind for just such a grouping. I just want to get a good feel for the shades of grey, like what the Cult of the living offers new members, what ceremonies they would learn/powers they would gain, how some would be more sympathic to Sin-eaters, while the far end of the spectrum would be perfectly happy with Tyrants view of their geists/the dead in general.<br /> <br /> Ghost eating by comparison seems a bit icky to me.<br /> <br /> Players guide also sounds awesome... Though i want things I can use in other games, so a book of the dead and interesting antagonists sounds great!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T07:41:08-07:00","id":1519110,"title":"","content":"I would also love more necromancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T11:13:12-07:00","id":1519120,"title":"","content":"Necromancers are good, yes. Maybe a couple Tier 2 / Tier 3 organizations that are flexible enough that the ultimate leadership could be swapped easily between Mages / Geists / Mortals as necessary.<br /> <br /> But there definitely needs to be one or two creatures that are just absolutely weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T15:28:58-07:00","id":1519127,"title":"","content":"I would personally prefer not to bring in hunter mechanics like tier or mage mechanics.<br /> <br /> Weird and creepy stuff though I'm down for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T17:28:58-07:00","id":1519136,"title":"","content":"Are there alien intelligences, are they worshipped, do we have Cults who try to feed their favourite new members to Chthonians? Or a group dedicated to follow the Old Laws or a particular dominion even while alive? That could have some creepy-ness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T17:49:09-07:00","id":1519139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1518349-\ud83d\udc7b-new-sin-eater-merits-\u2014-handbook-for-the-recently-deceased-preview?p=1519136#post1519136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there alien intelligences, are they worshipped, do we have Cults who try to feed their favourite new members to Chthonians? Or a group dedicated to follow the Old Laws or a particular dominion even while alive? That could have some creepy-ness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh ya, there's an infinite amount of room for creepiness in Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:50:56-07:00","id":1519213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1518349-\ud83d\udc7b-new-sin-eater-merits-\u2014-handbook-for-the-recently-deceased-preview?p=1519136#post1519136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a group dedicated to follow the Old Laws or a particular dominion even while alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Dominion which compels people to follow its laws even after they leave would be cool. It could either be from very weird Old Laws, an overenthusiastic Kerberos, or maybe a Kerberos recruiting a conspiracy for its personal goals.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dominions with strange laws are actually a rich area to explore. Maybe a Dominion with &quot;contradictory&quot; laws where everyone who goes there is able to follow the laws correctly, but is unable to explain or understand how the contradiction is handled once they leave.<br /> <br /> Edit2: I wrote up my &quot;contradictory&quot; Dominion.<br /> <br /> <b>The Obsidian Opacity</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>There\u2019s very little reliable information about the Dead Dominion known as Obsidian Opacity. Scholars who study it portray it as a realm of paradox and incongruity. Its landscape is described as a juxtaposition of haunting beauty and terror, featuring massives courtyards and parade grounds of polished lead out of which monolithic towers of black obsidian rise. These towers reach high into the cavernous ceiling and are lit from above by an otherworldly golden glow.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Upon entry, visitors receive a telepathic message from the Obsidian Scepter, the omnipresent lawgiver of the realm. Visitors describe this message as describing a set of laws so intricate and complex that they seem to warp reality itself. Only those who consciously commit to resisting this effect before entering the Opacity may try. This provokes a Clash of Wills in which the Scepter rolls twenty dice. It is widely agreed that the attempt is a violation of the Dominion\u2019s Old Laws, but this is difficult to confirm.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Obsidian Scepter stands tall in the center as the only tower to connect to the roof. Those within the Dominion know the distance and direction to the Scepter through whatever sense or intuition feels most appropriate. It thumps with an unseen heartbeat and pulsates with an ominous silver luminescence.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Old Laws, known to the poetic as the Enigma Edicts, are an enigma indeed. They are encoded in a language which noone aside from the Scepter is known to understand. The exact number of laws is debated with 1, 8, 12, 20, 160, and 240 as the most accepted answers. To the dwellers and visitors within Obsidian Opacity, they make perfect sense. Everyone seems to follow them without question or hesitation. Strangely, though, once an individual steps outside the Opacity's boundaries and loses contact with the Scepter, they realize that the Enigma Edicts are full of contradictions, impossibilities, and paradoxes that simply should not make sense.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Despite this, they remember following the edicts flawlessly, even if they can no longer comprehend or elucidate how such contradictory laws could function. It's as if the kingdom has a reality of its own that only makes sense within its borders, and to understand it from outside its confines is an effort in futility.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>This bewildering phenomenon has made the Obsidian Opacity an object of keen interest for many of the more esoteric necromancers. Aside from trading information on the shortcuts to the place, they use a variety of scrying and precognitive techniques, send in knowing and unknowing spies and convene in secret conferences where they mostly peacefully try to decipher the enigma from the safety of the world outside. Yet all but the most obsessed grow frustrated by the veil of mystery that shrouds Obsidian Opacity.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Note for Storytellers:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A mysterious mystery makes for nice fluff, but what if you want an actual answer? It would be rude of me not to explain a bit of what I was thinking. The Obsidian Scepter is, in fact, a Kerberos. It\u2019s supposed to be a magic artifact, most likely with a geist controlling it on behalf of whoever made it. The language is either entirely made-up, some ancient language that not even ghosts remember how to speak, or a variation of First Tongue or Atlantean. The number of laws is a mystery, both because noone understands the language, but because they are encoded as a single grid with twenty columns and twelve rows. There are eight main rows and four minor rows. The columns describe situations, the rows describe broad general purpose rules, with the cell going into detail of how that rule applies to the situation, and the Scepter interpreting how ambiguities in the table should be handled. It shouldn\u2019t be that hard to see why some might describe that as \u201c1, 8, 12, 20, 160, or 240\u201d rules.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Who made it? Either a Deathlord or a long gone krewe.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Could this Deathlord be a powerful Mage the Awakening NPC? I gave some hints to that by making some references to Stygia and the Watchtower of the Lead Coin, but the confusing nature of the place might be due to Abyssal influence.</b><br /> <br /> <b>How should this be used in a story? The Scepter and its Dominion are intended to either be background filler for a story dealing with other things or a puzzle for a group of experienced characters. Whoever made the place is not intended to show up and the Dominion is not something that players should try to brute-force.</b><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","user":"jsnider3","date":".  Obsidian Opacity 07-30-2023, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T14:00:01-07:00","id":1519282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1518349-\ud83d\udc7b-new-sin-eater-merits-\u2014-handbook-for-the-recently-deceased-preview?p=1519213#post1519213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Who made it? Either a Deathlord or a long gone krewe.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Could this Deathlord be a powerful Mage the Awakening NPC? I gave some hints to that by making some references to Stygia and the Watchtower of the Lead Coin, but the confusing nature of the place might be due to Abyssal influence.</b><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this Mage NPC, probably a Master of Death, with several other powers, went to the Underworld following an Obsession, maybe have gone a bit loopey living down there.<br /> <br /> May have summoned Stygian entities to try and turn a dominion into a representation of Stygia in the Fallen. Maybe have accidentally summoned an Abyssal entity instead. Whatever happened they are no longer present leaving the Obsidian Sceptre in place to keep running the place (or maybe she crafted her soul and body into the Sceptre). Either way, things do not appear to be running the way she intended.<br /> <br /> And while she likely left some research notes to explain how things are <i>meant</i> to be, but if they can't be found or understood (if other mages have them they can be kinda averse to sharing info with non-awakened, of course they may have been destroyed and be somewhere else in the Underworld) then she could be found, though whether she appear more like a Chthonian or even remembers anything of this Dominion will depend heavily on how deep into the Underworld she ended up (the Ocean of Fragments may have absorbed all her memories).<br /> <br /> Is she a true Deathlord now? Soul-Shaped into an unrecog usable form? Maybe she never was a Mage in the first place... In any case, there are numerous hooks their for your plot to grab onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  fixing grammar and typos 08-25-2023, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T09:52:48-07:00","id":1521390,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to check in and see how these books are coming along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}